## 🔍 Key Questions

The project aims to answer questions such as:

> Which products and categories generate the most revenue?

> Where are customers dropping out of the purchase funnel?

> Which products receive high traffic but have poor conversion?

> Which customers generate the highest observed revenue?

> How does customer retention change across acquisition cohorts?

> Which brands and categories have the strongest purchase performance?

> How does customer behavior vary over time?

> What customer segments can be identified using RFM analysis?

---

## ⚠️ Important Modeling Assumptions

The project explicitly documents analytical assumptions instead of treating them as source-system facts.

For example, the source dataset does not provide a traditional explicit order ID. Therefore, order-level metrics may use `user_session` as an **analytical proxy**, with this limitation clearly documented.

Similarly, event-level, session-level, customer-level and product-level analyses are kept at their respective grains to avoid accidental double counting.

